#
# VM targets are NOT pinned here. The cloud image ships no host keys;
# every guest generates fresh ones on first boot (sshd-keygen@*.service),
# so no VM key can be committed in advance. Instead the provisioner
# seeds a per-VM pin file at vm-test/results/known-hosts/<vm-name>
# (gitignored) by reading the keys out-of-band from the VM's own qcow2
# image (cp + virt-cat, never over the network), and the connection is
# pinned with -o HostKeyAlias=<vm-name> against that file. A VM without
# a pin file is refused; the harness never falls back to
# verification-off. To pin a target manually, add lines of the form
#   <name-or-ip> <key-type> <base64-key>
# using ssh-keyscan output, and connect to it by that name.
#
